 "text": "Hey, how are you doing? That's a lovely idea. Are there any small projects you' like to tackle together, like a box of fudge or a knitted bag? It is. You split it open on your doorstep and they' know it's from you. A card saying why you wanted to share it is nice too. One bar of chocolate and some sweeties comes to less than ten pounds, so it's affordable and feels special. Keep it in a drawer or cupboard you need to reach, and give the lid code as the password if someone asks to get in. Most people never go beyond the simple locked cabinet.",
